HST Office on Windows: does not register LibreOffice's vnd.libreoffice.command URI scheme.

The MSI registered HKCR\vnd.libreoffice.command as a URL protocol opening HST's soffice.exe and
named it in Capabilities\URLAssociations. With both suites installed, the last installer took the
scheme, and uninstalling either deleted it. Nothing in HST Office (help, start center, extensions,
links in documents) needs the scheme from Windows.

- The vnd.libreoffice.command protocol key and its URLAssociations entry are gone.
- The Office URI schemes (ms-word, ms-excel, ms-powerpoint, ms-visio) in HST's Capabilities point
  to the new ProgID HSTOffice.OfficeURI (open command, icon; no "URL Protocol" value, so it is not
  a scheme itself). The conditional ms-* protocol keys are unchanged.
- The office still accepts vnd.libreoffice.command: URIs on its command line (desktop cmdlineargs).

License: modified upstream files keep their license (MPL-2.0).

--- a/scp2/source/calc/registryitem_calc.scp
+++ b/scp2/source/calc/registryitem_calc.scp
@@ -1284,4 +1284,4 @@
 
 // registering ms-excel URI scheme handler
 CONDITIONAL_REGISTER_URI_HANDLER( ms-excel, ms_excel, gid_Module_Prg_Calc_MSO_Reg, SELECT_EXCEL )
-REGISTRY_ENTRY_CAPABILITIES_URL(ms-excel, ms_excel, gid_Module_Prg_Calc_MSO_Reg, vnd.libreoffice.command)
+REGISTRY_ENTRY_CAPABILITIES_URL(ms-excel, ms_excel, gid_Module_Prg_Calc_MSO_Reg, HSTOffice.OfficeURI)
